Visual language

Typography: Inter for UI, JetBrains Mono (or IBM Plex Mono) for all numbers, dates, and scores. Mono numerals give the dashboard its technical feel.
Surfaces: Bento-grid dashboard, 14–18px radii, glass cards with backdrop-filter: blur(12px), a faint dot-grid or noise texture on the canvas.
Signature details: Corner-bracket HUD marks on the hero score card, live “system status” dots (e.g., “Local data synced”), thin gradient rules, and conic-gradient match rings.
Motion: Framer Motion only. Count-up numbers, staggered card entrance (40ms steps), spring-based ring fills, 150–200ms hover transitions. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
Restraint rules: One glow per screen, max. No neon text. No decorative gradients behind body copy. Contrast must meet WCAG AA.

